","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T19:36:33+00:00","id":"hr1109-119","introducedDate":"2025-02-07","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-11-19","text":"Committee Consideration and Mark-up Session Held"},"laws":[],"number":"1109","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Law","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"I000056","district":48,"fullName":"Rep. Issa, Darrell [R-CA-48]","party":"R","state":"CA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-02-07","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Litigation Transparency Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill generally requires parties in a civil&nbsp;action&nbsp;to disclose to the court and other named parties the identity of any person (other than counsel) that has a right to receive a payment or thing of value contingent upon the outcome of the civil action. The bill also requires parties to produce the agreement creating the contingent right to payment or a thing of value.</p><p>These requirements apply to claims that are pending on or commenced after this bill's date of enactment.</p>","updateDate":"2026-09-09T17:10:26Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Litigation Transparency Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-09T17:11:02Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-09T17:11:02Z"}
